				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "#How the size is computed"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T16:00:45.062168+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T18:33:38.724621+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "suPGVqESQf6KtByCM7ArCA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Each page and snippet, and then the database itself, is a root of the estimation. Each root is split into categories by an attribution ({{gtClass:GtMemorySpaceAttribution}}): for example, the object in the slot `text` of a snippet, and everything reachable from it, goes to the Text category. A {{gtClass:GtMemorySpaceEstimator}} walks the objects and counts every object once, in the category of the first slot that reaches it. The walk stops at other pages and snippets, databases, classes, methods, symbols, announcement subscriptions and UI objects. The sizes are estimates: shared objects are attributed to the first category that reaches them."
			},
